      "source": [
        "## 5. Model architecture\n",
        "\n",
        "**DistilRoBERTa-base** is the compressed version of RoBERTa (6 transformer layers, hidden size 768, 12 heads, about 82 million parameters).\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Self-attention:** each token is represented by weighting all the other tokens: $\\text{softmax}(QK^\\top/\\sqrt{d_k})V$. For this reason the model can see that `not` relates to `good` even if they are several words apart (something bag-of-words cannot do).\n",
        "* **RoBERTa** compared to BERT: longer training on more data, no NSP task, and dynamic masking. With the byte-level BPE tokenizer, it handles spelling mistakes and emoji without `[UNK]`.\n",
        "* **Distillation:** the small model (student) is trained by imitating the output of the large model (teacher); about 95% of the quality with half the layers and ~2x the speed, which matters for free Colab.\n",
        "* **Fine-tune:** a 5-class classification head (dense → tanh → linear) is added to the representation of the first token (`<s>`) and the **whole network** is trained with a small learning rate (3e-5) on the data of this very domain (Amazon electronics product reviews); output = argmax over the 5 classes.\n",
        "* **Loss:** plain Cross-Entropy. (It ignores the ordering of the stars; in the error analysis section we see that mistakes are mostly between neighboring stars.)\n",
        "* **Optimization:** AdamW + 6% linear warmup then linear decay of the learning rate, gradient clipping = 1, mixed precision (fp16) for speed and memory, and equal-length batching (less padding) for speed."
      ]
    },
    {
