        "### What is an embedding and where does it happen in this model?\n",
        "\n",
        "A neural network only understands numbers, not words. **Embedding** means mapping each token to a numeric vector (here 768 numbers) such that tokens with similar meaning/usage have vectors close to each other. The steps in our model:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Text → tokens → numeric ID (token id) with the tokenizer.\n",
        "2. **Embedding table** (a 50,265 × 768 matrix): the row at the id's index is that token's vector. This table comes from RoBERTa's initial training and is also updated during our fine-tuning.\n",
        "3. A position vector (the token's place in the sentence) is added to it.\n",
        "4. Six self-attention layers refine these vectors with respect to the rest of the sentence (a \"contextual\" embedding).\n",
        "5. The `<s>` token's vector goes to the 5-class classification layer.\n",
        "\n",
        "We have not built a separate embedding (word2vec, GloVe or sentence-transformers); the embedding table is part of the model itself and is trained along with it. The cell below shows steps 1 and 2."
